    "id": "advanced-psy-23",
    "s": "Advanced Practice - Psychology",
    "module": 2,
    "q": "Participants startle normally to a loud sound. After repeated sound–image pairings, controls also show anticipatory arousal to the image. A lesion group can describe the pairing but shows little anticipatory arousal. What dissociation is most informative?",
