    "a": 5,
    "hint": "Identical wording does not guarantee that a measure has the same meaning in every context.",
    "e": "Comparisons require that the construct and indicators function sufficiently similarly across groups. Cognitive interviews, contextual adaptation and subgroup analyses can identify meaning differences before scores are compared as if equivalent.",
