    "hint": "Consider sample size, range restriction, measurement and the population to which the result applies.",
    "e": "A null finding may reflect a true absence, limited statistical power, restricted variation or measurement limitations. It should be reported with uncertainty and bounded to the sampled population rather than treated as universal proof.",
