    "a": 5,
    "hint": "Helping often involves several decision steps, and barriers can interrupt any stage.",
    "e": "Bystander models describe steps including noticing, interpreting an emergency, assuming responsibility, knowing how to help and acting. Ambiguity, diffusion of responsibility and lack of skills can interrupt different steps.",
