      "Unpaid work has no economic or political effects, using entry into paid employment as the principal evidence of improved economic position",
      "Family practices cannot be sociological evidence",
      "A value-free approach requires ignoring unpaid work; this follows from using entry into paid employment as the principal evidence of improved economic position",
      "Only wage labour can structure inequality, using recorded earnings to summarise employment quality and the worker’s resulting economic position",
      "Gender is a biological constant that needs no analysis"
