    "a": 3,
    "hint": "Focus on face-to-face interaction and the meanings participants use in that situation.",
    "e": "Micro-sociology analyses interaction, shared meanings and situational norms. The pattern suggests relational expectations about proximity, though broader claims require observations across people and settings.",
