    "hint": "The history of a discipline can be cumulative and contested rather than a simple succession of replacements.",
    "e": "Sociology's development involves debates, revisions and continuing use of classical insights, alongside critiques and new frameworks. Multiple perspectives do not make evidence irrelevant; they make assumptions and explanatory scope important to compare.",
