    "a": 4,
    "hint": "Structure and meaning need not be treated as mutually exclusive explanations.",
    "e": "Structural analysis examines organised relations and constraints, while interpretive analysis investigates meanings actors attach to conduct. Both can contribute if the researcher specifies how the evidence supports each claim.",
