    "a": 3,
    "hint": "Separate economic resources from prestige, power and context-specific recognition.",
    "e": "Social status can involve multiple dimensions and vary by setting. Income is informative about economic resources but cannot automatically represent prestige, education, authority or locally recognised influence.",
