    "a": 0,
    "hint": "A brief observation in one context cannot establish persistence, impairment or cross-setting patterns.",
    "e": "Behaviour varies with setting, age and immediate conditions. A defensible assessment considers persistence, impairment, multiple informants and alternative explanations rather than converting one observation into a diagnosis.",
