    "a": 2,
    "hint": "Receiving tactile input and recognising what it represents are separate processing steps.",
    "e": "Sensation detects physical input; perception organises and interprets it. A person may register touch but have difficulty recognising or naming the object, so assessment should distinguish sensory function from recognition and language access.",
