      "Treat consistent scores across administrations as evidence that the instrument accurately measures the intended psychological characteristic",
      "Prefer the instrument with the more detailed profile and interpret differences between tests as genuine changes in the person's traits",
      "Use agreement between raters to establish that the score is clinically meaningful across settings and suitable for diagnostic decisions",
      "Interpret the score using the available norms, treating translation and familiarity with the testing format as matters of presentation",
