    "a": 3,
    "hint": "A longitudinal view helps separate enduring patterns from changes linked to an episode.",
    "e": "Personality patterns are understood over time and across contexts, while an acute mood episode can temporarily alter behavior and self-report. Longitudinal assessment helps disentangle these influences; both may coexist.",
