    "a": 5,
    "hint": "The bystander may infer the event is not serious and assume someone else will act.",
    "e": "Pluralistic ignorance can lead a person to read others' inaction as evidence that there is no emergency, while diffusion of responsibility reduces felt personal obligation. A specific call to act can counter both.",
