    "a": 3,
    "hint": "The stated motivation centers on the other person's distress, not recognition.",
    "e": "Empathy-altruism accounts propose that empathic concern can motivate helping directed toward another's welfare. Motives are difficult to isolate experimentally, and multiple motives may coexist.",
