    "a": 5,
    "hint": "Assessing who is missed requires a denominator and characteristics of both reached and unreached households.",
    "e": "Comparing the eligible caseload with actual visits can reveal systematic exclusion by distance or vulnerability. Total visit counts alone can mask convenience selection and inequitable reach.",
