      "Repeat the same measures in the existing groups and treat a stable association as sufficient evidence of the proposed causal direction.",
      "Restrict analysis to participants who completed the programme successfully, so differences in engagement contribute less to the effect estimate.",
      "Selection and reverse causation may make the association look stronger than the visit effect",
