      "Compare the results before and after the activity and treat the observed change as the effect of the service delivered during that period",
      "Use the number of completed contacts as the principal outcome, interpreting increased activity as evidence that the underlying need has improved",
      "Ask staff to identify the cases that benefited most and use those examples to estimate the programme's likely effect for the wider population",
      "Measure satisfaction at the final contact and treat a favorable rating as evidence of sustained improvement after the intervention",
      "Compare participants who completed the programme with those who left early, treating the difference as the benefit of full participation"
